::recipe

name: Carbonara
source: https://publicdomainrecipes.com/carbonara/
source author: Peter Piontek, Ladislao Blanchi
source license: Public domain (Unlicense)
ingredients: mixed
units: mixed
category: main
tags: pasta, Italian
serves: 4
active time: ~5m
total time: ~30m
image: carbonara.webp

::ingredients

(spaghetti) 320g / 11oz
(egg, medium) 5

(pork) =
    (guanciale, cleaned, cubed) 150g / 5oz
    -OR-
    (smoked pancetta, cleaned, cubed) 150g / 5oz

(cheese, grated, optional) =
    (pecorino romano, grated, optional) ~35g + extra for serving
    -OR-
    (parmigiano-reggiano, grated, optional) ~35g + extra for serving

(black pepper, optional) to taste
(extra virgin olive oil, conditional) a dash
(salt) as needed

::equipment

(bowl)
(pot)
(pan, iron or non-stick)
(fork)

::instructions

(egg: yolk) <separate, bowl>

Optional [
    (egg: yolk) + (cheese) ~35g + (black pepper)
        <mix>
]

(pot) <fill, water>
    + (salt)
    <boil>

(spaghetti) <cook, 1m less than packet instructions>

(pork) <fry, pan, low-medium heat, until crisp outside and chewy inside>

# The source suggests a dash of olive oil only if using a different kind of pan.
Optional [
    (extra virgin olive oil) <add, pan>
]

Meanwhile [
    (egg: yolk) <beat, fork, until liquid>
]

(spaghetti) <drain>
    <rest, ~1m if too hot>

{carbonara} =
    (spaghetti) +
    (egg: yolk) +
    (pork)

{carbonara} <stir, continuously, with as much rendered pork fat as desired>

Optional [
    {carbonara} + (cheese) extra for serving + (black pepper)
        <garnish>
]

{carbonara} <serve>

::notes
The source notes that ingredient quality matters and recommends bronze-extruded pasta,
well-aged Italian cheeses, butchered guanciale and good eggs.